-- title:
--   Flatness over the base of the subscheme cut out by a Hilbert-functor point
-- statement:
--   Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$, a commutative ring $A$, a function $h : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$, and a point $p$ of the Hilbert functor of type $h$ over $A$, that is: an ideal $p.I$ of $A[X_0,\dots,X_n]$ that contains every homogeneous component of each of its elements, such that for every degree $d$ the $A$-module $\mathrm{piece}\ p.I\ d$, namely the degree-$d$ homogeneous submodule of $A[X_0,\dots,X_n]$ modulo its intersection with $p.I$, is finite and projective and has rank $h(d)$ at every prime of $A$. Let $\mathcal{I}$ be ideal sheaf data on $\mathrm{Proj}$ of the graded algebra of homogeneous submodules of $A[X_0,\dots,X_n]$, and assume that for each $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$ the ideal attached to $\mathcal{I}$ on the affine basic open $D_+(X_i)$ is generated by the sections `Proj.awayToSection` of the homogeneous localisations $F/X_i^{d}$, taken over all $d$ and all $F \in p.I$ homogeneous of degree $d$. The conclusion is that the closed immersion $\mathcal{I}.\mathrm{subscheme}\iota$ followed by `ProjSpace.π A n` is a flat morphism of schemes.
--
--   This is the flatness over the base of the closed subscheme of $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ cut out by a point of the Hilbert functor, with no restriction on the Hilbert function $h$ and no Gotzmann-type bound. It feeds the existence statements producing, for a point of the Hilbert functor, a closed immersion into $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ that is flat over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and whose ideal is described by $p.I$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_HilbertFunctor_Point_flat_comp_of_ideal_basicOpen_eq_span.lean

